# Contributing

Thank you for improving AiOps. Contributions should preserve the repository’s integration-backed operating model: operational records, telemetry, incident state, action results, and model responses must come from configured sources or be reported as unavailable.

## Development setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/RajaMuhammadAwais/AiOps.git
cd AiOps
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install black flake8 mypy build
```

Set the required `AIOPS_*` process environment before importing the application. The exact contract is documented in [README.md](README.md) and [INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md](INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md). Do not commit credentials, real customer data, upstream responses, or local environment files.

## Required checks

Run the same checks used by CI:

```bash
python -m compileall -q web_dashboard.py src tests
python -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_operational_foundations.py' -v
black --check web_dashboard.py src/platform src/alerting/alert_manager.py src/automation/intelligent_orchestrator.py src/deployment/aiops_orchestrator.py src/intelligence/predictive_engine.py src/ml/advanced_analytics.py tests/test_operational_foundations.py
flake8 src/platform tests/test_operational_foundations.py --max-line-length=100 --extend-ignore=E203,E501,E402,E722,W293 --count --show-source --statistics
mypy src/platform --ignore-missing-imports
python -m build
```

## Implementation rules

New integrations must define a bounded request and response contract, validate external payloads, propagate a structured unavailable result, and avoid silently substituting local values. Any action that changes external state must be routed through an explicitly configured executor and must not use arbitrary local shell execution.

Browser-facing values must be inserted as text or otherwise safely encoded. Do not add `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, `document.write`, unsafe template interpolation, or client-side evaluation of upstream content. Keep request limits, authentication behavior, audit redaction, and correlation identifiers intact.

Configuration belongs in `src/platform/config.py` and must be supplied through environment or a deployment secret manager. Do not embed endpoint URLs, credentials, operational thresholds, incident records, model output, or environment-specific service identities in executable source.

## Pull requests

A pull request should explain the operational problem, the changed integration contract, the security implications, the rollback behavior, and the validation performed. Include tests for unavailable integrations and malformed external responses when changing adapter or route behavior. Keep changes narrowly scoped and update the relevant operational documentation.

The protected branch workflow runs with read-only permissions for validation. Release publication is tag-gated and depends on successful validation and package generation.
